#
# uClibc install — yi-hack-v6
#
# We ship OUR uClibc 0.9.33.2 core libs into the rootfs /lib, overwriting the stock ones.
# This is NOT cosmetic: the stock Xiaomi ld-uClibc was built WITHOUT working LD_PRELOAD
# support, while ours has LDSO_PRELOAD_ENV_SUPPORT=y. The IPC multiplexer (ipc_multiplex.so,
# LD_PRELOAD'd into `dispatch` by system.sh) depends on LD_PRELOAD, so with the stock linker
# it silently never loads and the ipc_dispatch_N queues are never created -> mqttv4/ipc2file
# can't attach. Shipping our ld.so fixes that. (Proven on hardware: a test binary with
# PT_INTERP=our-ld.so honours LD_PRELOAD; the same with the stock linker does not.)
#
# ld.so and libc are a matched pair (shared link-map/TLS internals), so we ship our libc
# (libuClibc) alongside our ld.so. Our libuClibc is actually ~37 KB SMALLER than stock, so the
# rootfs (mtd4, 1280 KB, tight) net SHRINKS - these three are already present as stock real
# files, we only overwrite them. libm comes along to complete the core set.
#
# Partition split (rootfs can't hold the full uClibc set alongside busybox): only the CORE
# (ld-uClibc / libc / libm) lives in rootfs; the rest (librt / libdl / libpthread / ...) lives
# in /home/lib and is found via LD_LIBRARY_PATH at full boot. We do NOT add those to rootfs.
#
# libutil + libcrypt: the ONLY two uClibc libs stock never shipped (it had no SSH); dropbear
# NEEDs them. v5 offloaded them onto the SD with a /lib symlink that dangled in diskless v6
# (bug #1) - we ship them as real files here.
#
# Each lib = real .so + versioned-soname symlink. jffs2 supports symlinks (the 155-entry
# busybox farm relies on it); nothing here is staged onto FAT, so v5's "materialize every
# soname as a full copy to survive FAT" dance is gone.

SCRIPT_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
cd "$SCRIPT_DIR"

DEST=../../build/rootfs/lib
mkdir -p "$DEST"

# ship_lib <real-so> <soname>: real object + soname symlink. rm -f first so a partial/dirty
# rebuild (stale dangling link, or overwriting a stock symlink) can't make `cp` write through.
ship_lib() {
    rm -f "$DEST/$1" "$DEST/$2"
    cp -a "./_install/lib/$1" "$DEST/$1" || exit 1
    ln -sfn "$1" "$DEST/$2"              || exit 1
}

# Core (overwrites stock; our ld.so has working LD_PRELOAD):
ship_lib ld-uClibc-0.9.33.2.so ld-uClibc.so.0
ship_lib libuClibc-0.9.33.2.so libc.so.0
ship_lib libm-0.9.33.2.so      libm.so.0

# Stock never shipped these (dropbear/SSH needs them):
ship_lib libutil-0.9.33.2.so   libutil.so.0
ship_lib libcrypt-0.9.33.2.so  libcrypt.so.0
